            "short_description": {
                "apollo": "Film France-CNC is the French Film Commission and a department of the CNC (Centre national du cinéma et de l'image animée). Established in 1946, it serves as a key resource for foreign productions and individuals looking to film in France. The organization operates with legal and financial autonomy and is publicly owned.\n\nFilm France-CNC provides a range of services for international filmmakers and production companies. It offers production support and promotion, tax rebate management with potential rebates of up to 40%, location scouting, logistics assistance, and regulatory guidance. The organization also supports XR and video game projects. Led by Daphné Lora, the team includes specialists in various areas to assist with the needs of filmmakers. As part of the CNC, Film France-CNC contributes to the promotion and regulation of cinematic and audiovisual arts in France and is affiliated with the AFCI and the EuFCN Network.",
